      "writtenOn": "2017-04-05T14:50:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Location: the UID is needed to be enforced elsewhere as well. There are 2 places:\n\n1. In the factory (don\u0027t create network for a masquerading requestor): so the NS has to contain the UID to be used in the factory\n\n2. In the service (don\u0027t return a created network to a masquerading requestor)\n\nMutability: it isn\u0027t NetworkSpecifier which is abstract - it is whatever concrete derived class.\n\nSetting: having WifiAwareNetworkSpecifier constructed on the app side with the correct ID is invalid. You can\u0027t trust anything the app sends you. It must be done on the service side.",
      "parentUuid": "4417557d_3d35bfa7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4136,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 4136,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "c9cb890dfde49bece3f878d4e7a429a6c9fe4994",
